10. (Currently Amended) A control method of-tthe multifunctional electric wave generator for simulation of brain wave according to claim 1, comprising the following steps:

Step one: Ensuring the a power supply is stable, connecting the power and ground lines correctly, activating the electric wave generator and allowing it to warm up to improve-the frequency stability;

Step two: Selecting or setting a modulation mode as needed, -whieh--ineludes wherein the modulation modes are selected from the group of amplitude modulation, frequency modulation, and phase modulation, choosing appropriate filters to filter out clutter or noise fromthe an output signal, then-setting-Gr adjusting-various parameters,sueh--as wherein the parameters are selected from the group of waveform type, frequency, amplitude, through a microprocessor to ensure stable DC power supply to the an internal circuit of the electric wave generator body;

Step three: Selecting-the a desired waveform type through a waveform converter, which includes wherein the waveform type is selected from the group of sine wave, square wave, and triangle wave, setting-the a desired range of signal output frequency range by a frequency controller, adjusting a fine-tuning knob or a keyboard to input the a precise frequency, adjusting-the an output power of the power amplifier as needed to ensure sufficient signal strength, and monitoring-the waveform, frequency, amplitude, and other parameters of the output signal in real-time through a display device, utilizing a digital signal processor to further process and optimize the output signal.

